# Warp, end to end (CR 702.185a). Bot1 casts Pinnacle Emissary off one Island for its warp cost {U/R} on turn 1 — one
# hybrid mana, paid without a question — and the static ability on the stack creates a delayed triggered ability that
# exiles the permanent at the beginning of that turn's end step. Nothing goes on the stack for the creation, so Bot2
# never gets a window for it.
#
# It waits in exile until a later turn, where its owner casts it again for its real {1}{U}{R} and not for its warp cost
# a second time. Mishra's Bauble then gives it an artifact spell to see cast, and the Drone token it makes is a 1/1
# colourless artifact creature with flying that can block only creatures with flying: when Bot2's Fanatic of Rhonas
# (no flying, no reach) and Ornithopter (flying) attack on turn 6, the Drone may block the Ornithopter but not the Fanatic.

